// Starmote B: the land, the one source for both the terrain art and the collision mask.
//
// World pixels, y down. Each island is a closed chain of cubic Béziers (two control points, then
// the end), run clockwise on screen: walkable `Top`s left to right, `Rock` for cliffs, keels and
// crystals. Moon rock breaks in chunky facets, so keels are a few broad faces to a point. Tops are
// roughened along their normals and capped with star moss; rock stays smooth. `dress` places
// decorations into the map's terrain.svg, one rule per slot (`{{name}}`). Below the motes is
// only the void: whoever falls, or is dug out from under, is lost.
//
// B: a few larger motes. Two spawns a side on the big Spire Motes low at the edges and two on the
// High Shoals beside the middle, each pair either side of a crystal; between the shoals the
// Geode's spire stands up from below and the Lodestar hangs above. A stepping stone under each
// shoal's outer tip is the only land anything falls onto.
//
// This file was laid out from key points (the east half mirrors the west, with its own keels) and
// is the source from here on: edit it by hand.
Land(
    size: (2000, 1100),
    islands: [
        // Spire Mote: two spawns (130, 370) on the biggest mote, low at the west edge, either side
        // of a crystal outcrop; its west end grown into a tall crystal spire, a crystal under its
        // keel.
